Z||000009||86SE||01-08-2001||06:51 PM||||Its like trying to race a Porsche 911 Turbo against a Meclarin F1........about the same power difference.  No chance, don't even try it, you will be embarased.<P>But it does depend if the road has lots of curves, sharp ones, and the Fieros trans, mileage of both cars, how they have been driven over the years, etc......<P>You might KEEP UP with him til about 80-90, but after that, the HP difference kicks in and you are TOAST!<P>But does the Buick have a speed limiter lower than about 120?  If so, then you might take him over the long run....... <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://fierodude.hypermart.net/mysig.jpg"> <BR>'86 Special Edition,<BR>High-Output V-6 Yellow Fiero -- 3.4L Conversion *SUSPENDED* --<BR>Special Rally Heavy Duty Suspention||||reg||1
