Z||000014||Oreif||05-27-2001||10:14 PM||||I raced a guy from work with a 2000 GTP Grand Prix. Mine is a 2.8 Auto with headers and a shift kit on the trans. Everything else<BR>is stock. I got the jump off the line. I was probably ahead up until about 25-30 mph at that time the blower on his 3800 was producing plenty boost and away he went. The 3800SC's are very strong engines. Even though the Regal/Grand Prix weigh more, That just slows them off the line. Unless your racing on a tight course, don't waste the gas and try. If your car is stick shift, you may be able to stay ahead a little longer but not for long. ||||reg||1
Z||000015||Taijiguy||05-27-2001||11:11 PM||||Forget all that other hoorah. If you're planning the kind of race I think you're planning, then the post about who has the biggest kahuna's is accurate, and that's the guy who's gonna take the trophy. <BR>We used to run races like that in Michigan, Virginia Beach, and Charleston. Road rally type races. The beauty part of those isn't just the power of a car, but the skill of the driver, and luck in avoiding law enforcement. Unfortunately, I haven't run across too many Ohio State cops with a real sense of humor about road racing. Things are alot different than they used to be.||||reg||1
